PHPDoc-only types were missing from both production graphs: for example, `@return list<Item>` did not make its declaration depend on `Item`, even when the engine-equivalence tests passed.

This change parses PHPStan's annotation grammar with the standalone `phpstan/phpdoc-parser` library and records `phpdoc` dependencies (`phpDoc` in GQL), including annotation lines and byte offsets. Both engines share the documentation pass, with matching support for namespace imports, templates, local and imported type aliases, shapes, callables, conditional types, magic members, inheritance annotations, mixins and assertions. The experimental symbol graph retains its parity with native.

`tests/diff/` adds a `diff` PHPUnit suite, runnable with `composer test:diff` and included in the normal test run. Its 146 cases compare complete canonical graphs and assert concrete documented dependencies and attribution, including PHP 7.1–8.5 analysis targets. Native runs in a separate process so PHPStan's bundled PHPDoc parser cannot mask differences in the standalone parser. Negative cases cover malformed tags, unsupported prefixes, metadata, descriptions and shape keys.

These are dependencies written in documentation; the change does not synthesize magic method bodies or add PHPStan's control-flow type inference. The full PHPStan engine remains a development dependency. The PHAR packaging check now distinguishes that engine from the small PHPDoc parser library.

